ty). Also difficulty communicating ideas (communication). Egocentric (crew cooperation maybe issue, but we have positive atmosphere note). Not willing to further education (adaptability). So we have mixed.\n\nNow we need to contribute: maybe compare Candidate C to B, focusing on crew cooperation and responsibility, and note that C shows good crew cooperation but has communication issues and lack of adaptability. Also note that B's communication issue is pretentious tone. We might ask about Candidate D's communication style or temperament to compare. Or ask about Candidate A's openness to new ideas (we have private note: not open to new ideas). Could ask about D's crew cooperation. But we have limited tool calls; we can ask another agent.\n\nWe should share the new evidence about C's crew cooperation, and perhaps suggest that C's positive crew cooperation offsets some concerns, but his communication difficulty and lack of willingness to learn remain concerns. Then perhaps ask about Candidate D's crew cooperation or communication style to fill gap.\n\nThus public message: summarize that C shows strong crew cooperation, good decision making, calm under pressure, technical competence, but communication difficulty and lack of adaptability. Compare to B's strengths and concerns. Then propose next step: need info on D's crew cooperation and responsibility, or ask about D's temperament effect.\n\nWe also need to set our vote. Currently provisional recommendation was B from Agent 3. After seeing C's crew cooperation, does that change? B still strong but communication issue. C has crew cooperation but communication difficulty and egocentric, not willing to learn. B's communication issue is pretentious tone, maybe less severe? Hard to decide. I think still B is leading, but we need more info on D and A. So keep vote B.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
